# UBSan findings that are NOT this server's, with the reason each is here.
# A campaign that stops on somebody else's defect at run one is a campaign
# that never runs, and an -fno-sanitize= would turn the whole check off
# for our code too. This names the file and the check instead.
#
# ls-hpack, lshpack.c:236 - lshpack_arr_push's first growth does
#   memcpy(new, arr->els + arr->off, 0) with els == NULL and off == 0.
#   NULL + 0 is undefined even though the copy moves nothing, and it
#   fires on the FIRST dynamic-table insert of every h2 connection, which
#   is to say on the first h2 request a campaign sends. deps/ls-hpack is
#   a submodule pinned at upstream; this line goes when the pin moves
#   past a fix. #208 was the other kind - that one was ours.
#   The one line trips two checks: NULL + 0 is pointer-overflow, and
#   handing that to memcpy is nonnull-attribute.
pointer-overflow:lshpack.c
nonnull-attribute:lshpack.c
